This is the final piece of the puzzle for a perfect user experience!
Because your "Apply This Remark" checkbox already copies the text into every row's remarks field in the background, all we have to do is tell the Submit button to look at the rows and ask: *"Are all required fields and remarks filled out?"*
If any row is missing a valid remark (or a branch, currency, etc.), the button stays gray. The moment you check the box and those remarks copy down, the button will instantly turn green!
Here are the exact two steps to add this logic to JournalPosting.js.
### 1. Create the Form Readiness Check
Find the return ( statement where your JSX UI begins (around line 430, right after the handleSubmit function ends).
**Insert this logic right *above* the return statement:**
```javascript
    // ... end of handleSubmit function ...

    // NEW LOGIC: Check if EVERY row is completely filled, including the compulsory 2-30 char remarks
    const isFormReadyToSubmit = rows.every(
      (row) =>
        row.branch &&
        row.currency &&
        row.cgl &&
        row.amount &&
        row.txnType &&
        isRowRemarksValid(row.remarks)
    );

    return (
      <Box sx={{ p: 3, maxWidth: "98%" }}>

```
### 2. Update the Submit Button
Scroll to the very bottom of the file where the **Submit** button is located. We will add the new isFormReadyToSubmit check to the disabled property.
**Find this block:**
```javascript
            <Button
              variant="contained"
              color="success"
              onClick={handleSubmit}
              disabled={isSubmitting || !isCommonRemarksValid(commonBatchRemarks)}
            >
              {isSubmitting ? <CircularProgress size={24} /> : "Submit"}
            </Button>

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
            <Button
              variant="contained"
              color="success"
              onClick={handleSubmit}
              // Button is disabled if submitting, if common remarks are invalid, OR if any row is missing data/remarks!
              disabled={
                isSubmitting || 
                !isCommonRemarksValid(commonBatchRemarks) || 
                !isFormReadyToSubmit
              }
            >
              {isSubmitting ? <CircularProgress size={24} /> : "Submit"}
            </Button>

```
### How it works now:
 1. When you load the page, the Submit button is **disabled** because the first row doesn't have a remark yet.
 2. If you manually type a remark into Row 1 (along with the branch, amount, etc.), the Submit button **enables**.
 3. If you clear Row 1's remark, type "Monthly Adjustment" into the Common Batch Remarks, and click the **"Apply This Remark To All"** checkbox... React instantly copies "Monthly Adjustment" into Row 1, sees that all rows are now valid, and **instantly enables the Submit button!**
